WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.100
[music]

2
00:00:05.866 --> 00:00:09.733
[Instructor] Our score is now perfect
and ready to go

3
00:00:09.733 --> 00:00:12.566
so each time we click one
of the different objects

4
00:00:12.566 --> 00:00:14.600
that spawn,
it gives us a different number.

5
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:18.233
Which is a lot of fun,
you can see the score updates.

6
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:22.000
But it definitely doesn't
look or feel that cool

7
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.000
when you click on the different ones.

8
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.100
So we're going to up the coolness factor
by a lot by using some particle effects.

9
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:38.000
In our Target Script we're
going to create a new

10
00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:41.466
public variable, so we can
assign it in our editor.

11
00:00:41.833 --> 00:00:43.900
It'll be a "ParticleSystem."

12
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:50.366
We'll call this the "explosionParticle."

13
00:00:52.433 --> 00:00:55.833
Now we want to make sure
whenever we Destroy() one

14
00:00:55.833 --> 00:00:58.000
of our objects,
we use our explosionParticle.

15
00:00:59.466 --> 00:01:03.300
In our "OnMouseDown()" method,
we're going to create

16
00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:07.066
a new explosion every time
we Destroy(gameObject).

17
00:01:07.466 --> 00:01:11.766
We can actually Instantiate()
our explosionParticle.

18
00:01:12.933 --> 00:01:16.500
We'll set the position
to be the position

19
00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:18.333
that our current game object is at.

20
00:01:23.833 --> 00:01:27.633
And we'll just set the particle
to be at the same rotation

21
00:01:27.633 --> 00:01:29.733
that it was at before.

22
00:01:34.266 --> 00:01:38.766
Now in Unity, just make sure
that on each of the different Prefabs,

23
00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:44.600
you open them up and we need to assign
them each "Explosion Particles."

24
00:01:45.066 --> 00:01:47.666
If we open up our Course Library,

25
00:01:47.666 --> 00:01:50.766
we actually have some particle effects
that we can already use.

26
00:01:52.766 --> 00:01:58.233
I think for the case of our Skull,
we'll make it like a green color.

27
00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:00.500
See what that looks like.

28
00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:06.533
For our first good crate,
we'll make this something like yellow.

29
00:02:08.233 --> 00:02:14.800
For our second good crate,
we'll make this something like purple.

30
00:02:17.466 --> 00:02:19.500
And then for our third good crate,

31
00:02:20.733 --> 00:02:24.533
we'll make this something like,
let's make it blue.

32
00:02:26.966 --> 00:02:30.166
Now if we try our game again,

33
00:02:33.033 --> 00:02:39.600
we click on one box, there's purple,
yellow, this one should be green.

34
00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:45.766
Cool. Now we have these really
cool eye catching effects

35
00:02:45.766 --> 00:02:48.200
whenever we click on one
of the different Objects

36
00:02:49.066 --> 00:02:52.333
and just makes our game
feel a little bit cooler.

37
00:02:55.833 --> 00:02:58.533
So what you're gonna do,
is in your Target Script,

38
00:02:58.533 --> 00:03:02.233
you're going to create your own
"public ParticleSystem" variable.

39
00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:09.066
In your OnMouseDown() method,
where we Destroy() our Object,

40
00:03:09.633 --> 00:03:13.133
we are then going to create
a new explosion particle

41
00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:16.300
and we'll make sure to set
it to the current position

42
00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:18.300
of what our gameObject is at

43
00:03:18.666 --> 00:03:22.533
and make sure the rotation is the same
as the actual explosionParticle.

44
00:03:23.333 --> 00:03:26.400
And then in Unity,
just make sure you go to each

45
00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:29.566
of your different Prefabs and assign

46
00:03:29.666 --> 00:03:33.800
an Explosion Particle from
the Course Library folder

47
00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.600
in our particles folder,
where there are a variety

48
00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:40.466
of different explosions
that you can use. Now it's your turn.

49
00:03:42.366 --> 00:03:44.566
[music]
